9,Ndengereko / Ndengeleko,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Ndengereko.htm,"Other comments: Ndengereko or Ndengeleko, also known as Rufiji (Fiji, Ruihi) after the local river, spoken by approximately 72,000 people, is a Bantu language of the Matumbi hills, near Kibiti, and near Mchukivi and Bungu, Tanzania.",Ndengereko,Niger-Congo
